                <pb facs="0228" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg120"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 2.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson reports that the insurgents have withdrawn their restrictive orders,
                    that ships of all nationalities are no longer kept from coming to the shore, and
                    notes a favorable progress of commerce, all of which he says is due to the
                    influence of the war vessels of the United States having stopped the insurgents’
                    fire against American merchant vessels.</p>
            </div>
